XNU-4570 board bring-up patch 0001: ARM_MSMA53 machine + MSM8916 board
config for vivo Y35A (PD1502A).

Apply from the xnu-4570 tag checkout with:
    patch -p1 < patches/xnu4570/0001-y35a-board.patch

Build knob (see docs/board/ios12-bringup-map.md section 6 for the full
contract with the concurrent vanilla-build agent):
    ARCH_CONFIGS=ARM64 MACHINE_CONFIGS=MSM8916 -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MSM8916
    (the 4570 tag tree has no MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_* table at all -- the
    -D injection follows scripts/build-xnu-4903-kernel.py's established
    convention) -- plus CONFIG_REQUIRES_U32_MUNGING=1 (bsd_arm64.c:109).

Design invariant: MSM8916 mirrors Apple Typhoon (iPad mini 4) exactly --
__ARM_16K_PG__ absent (4K hardware granule), __ARM64_PMAP_SUBPAGE_L1__
present, and the 16K SOFTWARE page size arrives at runtime from
osfmk/arm/arm_init.c:178 because memSize > 1GB.  Do NOT add
__ARM_16K_PG__.  Do NOT define APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY: it is what keeps
every Apple-only c15/HID/PMGR/EL3-monitor sequence compiled out; A53 traps
on them.  The now-live non-Apple fallbacks (CleanPoU caches, fiq_context,
xcall questions, U32 munging) are implemented in patches 0002+, tracked in
docs/board/ios12-bringup-map.md section 3/4.  This patch alone is
board-definition only: it does NOT by itself make the kernel boot.

--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
@@ -102,8 +102,34 @@
 #endif  /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8011 */
 
 
+#ifdef ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MSM8916
+/*
+ * vivo Y35A (PD1502A): Qualcomm MSM8916, 4x Cortex-A53 r0p3 (MIDR
+ * 0x410fd030), armv8.0, GICv2 (qgic; GICD_TYPER=0x468, SecurityExtn set),
+ * ARM generic timer @19.2MHz (virtual timer INTID 20), 2GB RAM, 4K
+ * hardware page granule.  Every constant's provenance:
+ * docs/board/y35a-facts.md (stock QCDT platform 206 / variant 8 / subtype
+ * 23 + on-device readback probes).
+ *
+ * Page-size regime: hardware 4K + software 16K chosen at RUNTIME by
+ * osfmk/arm/arm_init.c:178 (memSize > 1GB -> PAGE_SHIFT_CONST =
+ * PAGE_MAX_SHIFT = 14).  This is byte-for-byte the shipping configuration
+ * of iPad mini 4 (Typhoon): Typhoon also omits __ARM_16K_PG__
+ * (osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h:126-140).  Never add __ARM_16K_PG__ to this block;
+ * see docs/board/ios12-bringup-map.md section 1 for the full verdict.
+ */
+#define ARM_MSMA53                   /* machine selector for
+                                      * osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h's new
+                                      * ARM_MSMA53 block */
+#define ARM_ARCH_TIMER
+#include <pexpert/arm64/MSM8916.h>
+#define __ARM_L2CACHE_SIZE_LOG__ 20     /* MSM8916 shared L2 = 1MB (stock DTB) */
+#define ARM_BOARD_WFE_TIMEOUT_NS 1000
+#define ARM_BOARD_CLASS_MSM8916
+#define CPU_COUNT 4
+/* KERNEL_INTEGRITY_WT deliberately absent: no Apple watchtower exists at
+ * our EL1 handoff.  MONITOR requirement (osfmk/arm64/cpu.c:794) is
+ * satisfied by NO_MONITOR in MSM8916.h. */
+#endif  /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MSM8916 */
 
